(Bursa rule)","src":"rule"}],"recent_en":"Betamek reported quarterly results for the period ended 30 September 2026, with revenue up 12.4% year-on-year to RM81.49 million but net profit down 32.1% year-on-year to RM7.07 million. The company declared a second interim dividend of 1.25 sen per share, with ex-date on 25 November. It also continued to issue new shares from the exercise of its Employees' Share Option Scheme (ESOS).","notable_en":["Declared a second interim dividend of 1.25 sen per share, with ex-date on 25 November 2026.","Announced quarterly results for the period ended 30 September 2026, with revenue up 12.4% year-on-year and net profit down 32.1% year-on-year.","Entered into a memorandum of understanding (MOU)."],"risks_en":["Independent Non-Executive Chairman Ahmad Subri bin Abdullah disposed of 100,000 ordinary shares in the open market.","Net profit fell 32.1% year-on-year, with net margin declining from 10.3% to 8.7%.","Continued issuance of new shares from ESOS exercises may dilute existing shareholders' equity."],"earnings_en":"For the quarter ended 30 September 2026, revenue was RM81.49 million, up 12.4% year-on-year and 2.1% quarter-on-quarter; net profit was RM7.07 million, down 32.1% year-on-year and 14.4% quarter-on-quarter; net margin was 8.7%, lower than 10.3% in the previous quarter."}